From: Michael Narine <michael@verita-ai.com>
Date: Fri, 09 Oct 2026 21:04:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Print: initialise PrintRegion::m_config_hash and FakeWipeTower members

PrintRegion::m_config_hash is set by the two constructors that take it and by set_config(), but
the default constructor and PrintRegion(const PrintRegionConfig &) leave it indeterminate. The
hash feeds region de-duplication in Print::apply, so an indeterminate value can merge or split
regions depending on what the allocator returned.

FakeWipeTower (a member of Print) has no initialisers: pos, width, height, layer_height, depth,
brim_width, rotation_angle, cone_angle and plate_origin hold garbage until
set_fake_extrusion_data() runs, and Print::first_layer_wipe_tower_corners and the exclude-object
code read some of them on prints without a wipe tower. Same class of bug as patches 0009 to
0012: the cube slice stays the same, but the value is no longer left to the allocator.

Value-initialise all of them (zero).

Purpose: Fix uninitialised members PrintRegion::m_config_hash and FakeWipeTower::{pos,width,height,layer_height,depth,brim_width,rotation_angle,cone_angle,plate_origin}.
SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
Upstream-Status: to be submitted
Orca-Base: v2.4.2
---
diff --git a/src/libslic3r/Print.hpp b/src/libslic3r/Print.hpp
--- a/src/libslic3r/Print.hpp
+++ b/src/libslic3r/Print.hpp
@@ -143,7 +143,7 @@
     friend int  print_region_ref_cnt(const PrintRegion&);

     PrintRegionConfig  m_config;
-    size_t             m_config_hash;
+    size_t             m_config_hash { 0 };
     int                m_print_region_id { -1 };
     int                m_print_object_region_id { -1 };
     int                m_ref_cnt { 0 };
@@ -593,16 +593,16 @@
 struct FakeWipeTower
 {
     // generate fake extrusion
-    Vec2f pos;
-    float width;
-    float height;
-    float layer_height;// Due to variable layer height, this parameter may be not right.
-    float depth;
+    Vec2f pos { Vec2f::Zero() };
+    float width { 0.f };
+    float height { 0.f };
+    float layer_height { 0.f };// Due to variable layer height, this parameter may be not right.
+    float depth { 0.f };
     std::vector<std::pair<float, float>> z_and_depth_pairs;
-    float brim_width;
-    float rotation_angle;
-    float cone_angle;
-    Vec2d plate_origin;
+    float brim_width { 0.f };
+    float rotation_angle { 0.f };
+    float cone_angle { 0.f };
+    Vec2d plate_origin { Vec2d::Zero() };
     Vec2f rib_offset{0.f,0.f};
     std::map<float , Polylines> outer_wall; //wipe tower's true outer wall and brim

